// Textual twin requires the same mapping here (not the engine's raw 256-index
// SGR, and not a style.Token — these are theme ANSI slots). Grouped charts
// auto-cycle the palette (series i → colorSequence[i] = blue+/green+/red+/…), so
// every slot a chart can reach needs an entry. Each hex is the ANSI palette
// index → RGB that Textual actually emits, read from that ANSI theme and
// cross-checked against the Textual-seeded golden (NOT a Go-accepted golden —
// that would validate a guess against itself). Production charts use ≤3 series
// (blue+/green+/red+); cyan+/magenta+ are included for completeness. Note the
// Monokai palette renders ANSI 9 (red) and ANSI 13 (magenta) as the same #F4005F.
//
